From 51c5650e5980fd04b5310402c726e59b9fec74d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 15:35:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] TS6: migrate signal spice from union bit-casts to native
 :float types

Drop defalias Sample :int and replace all C union { int64_t i; double d; }
bit-cast patterns with proper :float type annotations.

dsp.tur:
- __dsp_sin [x :float] :float -- return sin(x); no union
- __dsp_fmod [x :float y :float] :float -- return fmod(x, y); no union
- sine/square/sawtooth: outer params :float; inner closures use TS2 reinterpret
- low-pass/high-pass/gain: outer params :float; memcpy replaces unions
- mix/add: memcpy for Pair field extraction

envelope.tur:
- ADSRParams struct fields changed from :int to :float
- __adsr_fixed_sample: all params/return :float; no union

synth.tur:
- Removed (defalias Sample :int)
- __sample-add/mul now use native float arithmetic
- Float literal params: 0.01/0.1/0.5 etc. directly

arrow_tests.tur:
- __f_* helpers kept as :int for __arrow_call1 ABI
- DSP calls use (:: (__f_N) :float) casts
- Fixed missing closing parens in run-tests

